WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.490
- [Devin] The criminal
justice system is filled

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.010
with arcane legal terminology.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.970
Lay people often use this
vernacular incorrectly.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.510
- Habeas Corpus.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.410
- [Devin] They say bad law words.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.160
- Incredibly exact.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.583
- [Devin] But we can make
these bad law words good?

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.100
What actually is a chicken?

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.160
There's a whole debate over
whether a hot dog is a sandwich.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.550
That's generally how lay people sound

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.250
when they're using legal concepts.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.960
That defines a tomato as a fruit,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.793
even though we all know
a tomato is a vegetable.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.950
Malice aforethought,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:42.950
Good Samaritan law,

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.163
an offense against all the people.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.460
Right off the bat is begging the question.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.293
A catch 22.

00:00:49.293 --> 00:00:50.960
The Bed of Procrustes.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.150
Imminent and eminent.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.010
Insure versus ensure.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.630
And then there's forego versus forgo.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.480
Because I'm informed
that some of you actually

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.150
are not lawyers and that saddens me

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.670
so welcome to Bad Law Words Good.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.503
Legal Eagle.

